{"adjusted_val_bpb": 0.47315772771306563, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No sign of getting around the measurement. The edit only changes how the RF and SVR predictions are combined: it averages z-scores instead of normalized ranks. The mean and sd come from each model's own predictions on the test set, never from test labels. This is a fixed rescaling within each fold, so it is legitimate for a Spearman-based score.", "No bug that would make the result meaningless. The code returns one finite prediction per test molecule, and the 1e-9 term guards against dividing by zero.", "My z is close to the harness value. Candidate minus incumbent is 0.4732 - 0.4718 = 0.0014. With one run each and noise sd 0.0070, the sd of the difference is 0.0070*sqrt(2) \u2248 0.0099, which gives z \u2248 -0.14 (negative means the candidate is worse). The harness reports -0.137. The small gap is consistent with rounding of the displayed 4-decimal losses.", "The difference is well inside the noise, so the decision to reject is reasonable. The change brings no measurable gain, and the incumbent's rank average is equally simple."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Replace the final rank-sum blend with an equal-weight mean of each member's z-scored test predictions (XGBoost and Tanimoto SVR unchanged), so the output keeps each model's magnitude instead of ranking.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "spruce", "idea_id": "b015", "incumbent_after": {"mean": 0.4717979900923728, "n": 1}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": 0.4717979900923728, "n": 1}, "job_id": "B2_clear_SS_1_s0-candidate-7_1795070947417", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.0017633, "cost_usd_plan": 0.0017633, "latency_s": 4.423482811020222, "requested_model": "haiku", "role": "coder", "served_model": "haiku", "tokens_in": 7000, "tokens_out": 727}, {"cost_usd_nominal": 0.03622, "cost_usd_plan": 0